# VoiceForge AI — Monorepo .dockerignore
# Keep image small by excluding everything not needed for build/run.

# Dependencies
node_modules
**/node_modules
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
pnpm-debug.log

# Build outputs
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
out

# Git
.git
.gitignore
.github

# IDE
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Docker
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*
.dockerignore

# Docs (not needed at runtime)
docs
*.md
!README.md

# Test / local env.
#
# The `**/` prefixes matter and their absence was a real leak: Docker matches
# ignore patterns against the whole context-relative path, so a bare `.env`
# excludes only the root file and leaves `apps/api/.env` and
# `apps/web/.env.local` in the context — where `COPY apps/api apps/api`
# (Dockerfile.api) and `COPY apps/web apps/web` (Dockerfile.web) copy them into
# the build stage and `next build` reads `.env.local` automatically. Both files
# hold real secrets. Same reason `**/node_modules` above is not bare
# `node_modules`.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
coverage
.nyc_output

# Agent and CI scratch trees. Each is a full copy of the repository, several
# carry their own env files, and nothing in any Dockerfile copies from them —
# so they are pure build-context weight and pure secret exposure.
.worktrees
.claude
.depot
.work-tools

# Misc
*.log
*.tmp
*.temp
temp
tmp
